      "html": "† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">אָרַח</span></big></big>  <strong>v. peregrinar, viajar, ir (</strong>fenício <span dir=\"rtl\">ארח</span> em <span dir=\"rtl\">מארח</span>, provavelmente = <span dir=\"rtl\">מְאָרֵחַ</span>; cf. etiópico መርሐ <em>conduzir, guiar</em>; veja-se Nö<sup>ZMG 1888, 472</sup>; epíteto do deus Esmum, sabeu <span dir=\"rtl\">ארחֿ</span> DHM<sup>Epigr. Denkm. p. 70</sup>, aramaico <span dir=\"rtl\">אוֹרֵחַ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܳܪܚܳܐ</span> <em>viajante</em><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  perfeito: <span dir=\"rtl\">וְאָרַח</span> consecutivo <a data-ref=\"Job 34:8\" href=\"/Job.34.8\">Jb 34:8</a>; particípio: <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹרֵחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:17\" href=\"/Judges.19.17\">Ju 19:17</a> +; plural: <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹרְחִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:1\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.1\">Je 9:1</a>;—<strong>1.</strong>  <em>viajar, ir</em>, com <span dir=\"rtl\">עִם</span> figuradamente, indicando associação, companheirismo <a data-ref=\"Job 34:8\" href=\"/Job.34.8\">Jb 34:8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">וְא׳ לְחֶבְרָה עִם־פֹּעֲלֵי אָ֑וֶן וְלָלֶכֶת עִם־אַנְשֵׁי־רֶֽשַׁע׃</span> (cf. também <span dir=\"rtl\">הלך</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 1:1\" href=\"/Psalms.1.1\">ψ 1:1</a>).<strong>2.</strong>  particípio: <em>peregrinando, viajando, em viagem</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">הָאִישׁ הָאֹרֵחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:17\" href=\"/Judges.19.17\">Ju 19:17</a>; como substantivo: <em>peregrino, caminhante, viajante</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹרֵחַ</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:4\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.4\">2 S 12:4</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הֵלֶךְ</span>), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 14:8\" href=\"/Jeremiah.14.8\">Je 14:8</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּר</span>, em comparação com <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">מְלוֹן אֹרְחִים</span> <em>alojamento de viajantes</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:1\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.1\">Je 9:1</a>.",
