      "ordinal": 849,
      "headword": "אֲרַמִּי",
      "ref": "BDB, אֲרַמִּי",
      "preview": "אֲרַמִּי: arameu, gentílico; formas com artigo, plurais e variante de crítica textual.",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֲרַמִּי</span></big>  <strong>adj. gentílico arameu</strong>; com artigo <span dir=\"rtl\">הָא׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 25:20\" href=\"/Genesis.25.20\">Gn 25:20</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 28:5\" href=\"/Genesis.28.5\">28:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:20\" href=\"/Genesis.31.20\">31:20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 31:24\" href=\"/Genesis.31.24\">24</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 5:20\" href=\"/II_Kings.5.20\">2 K 5:20</a>; acerca de Israel, <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳ אֹבֵד</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:5\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.5\">Dt 26:5</a>; plural <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲרַמִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 8:28\" href=\"/II_Kings.8.28\">2 K 8:28</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 8:29\" href=\"/II_Kings.8.29\">29</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲרָם</span>), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 9:15\" href=\"/II_Kings.9.15\">9:15</a> (‖ <em>idem</em>); <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרַמִּים</span> (= <span dir=\"rtl\">הָא׳</span>) <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 22:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.22.5\">2 Ch 22:5</a> (‖ <em>idem</em>); <span dir=\"rtl\">פִּילַגְשׁוֹ הָאֲרַמִּיָּה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 7:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.7.14\">1 Ch 7:14</a> <em>sua concubina arameia</em>.—(<span dir=\"rtl\">ארומים</span>, Ketiv <a data-ref=\"II Kings 16:6\" href=\"/II_Kings.16.6\">2 K 16:6</a>; leia-se preferivelmente, segundo o Qerê, <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲדוֹמִים</span>).",
